Hello, everyone.

I would like to announce my candidacy for PTL of the Barbican project for
the 2027.1 cycle.

This would be my third year serving as PTL. Over the past cycle, the
project's focus shifted toward preparing Barbican for a post-quantum
world while continuing routine maintenance and modernization: we began
implementing crypto-agility in the SimpleCrypto plugin, and I proposed
and stood up the TC-approved PQC Migration pop-up team to coordinate
this effort across projects. We also worked on adopting Secure RBAC in
Barbican.

As in previous cycles, I kept up weekly patch reviews to keep the
review queue healthy and merge velocity steady, and led the bi-weekly
project meeting on IRC.

Thank you for your continued trust and support.

Mauricio Harley (mharley)
